# Wave W17-P (Route 119): gauge sand — rain-road sand: a darker sand than any dry road’s, puddle-polished — grey-blue sheen flecks stand in the tread where the rain keeps its own mirrors (design-authorised: a clear connected path running end to end, the ford road to Highbranch; split from Yamato’s rainfloor by the gorge register — darker base, polished puddle flecks, the Institute’s gauge dressing at its posts). The wettest road in Maris: it does not dry, it shines.
